{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact first-press head 626d8551b676a08203264552fbe4d5044850cc2d on builder/first-press-20261102, for request 368ddc87 and review request 14160c7b, with companion witness 9abee3a0.\n\nScope. Main 2950cff9 is an ancestor. The head adds five commits and changes 15 paths. 2f825e32 changes only packages/mcp/test/declared-members.test.ts relative to 3e2c000b, and 626d8551 adds only the note and the manifest after it. The worktree is clean, and the commit-message check passes for all five commits. Every other live artifact at .github/workflows, apps/views, docs, packages/mcp and scripts sits on main, so the head's artifacts retire only landed work.\n\nThe reduction. The Native owner witnesses the claim directly. In witness 4, the requests between a first View diff press and its act equal exactly four GETs: Membership, Directory, Rules and the destination. Then one read-token act follows. The retained runs agree. I regenerated the comparison with after-2/summarize.py --report, and it exits 0 with 12 requests before and four after in each of three first presses: 4,497.4 ms became 699.1 ms, 1,779.5 ms became 308.1 ms, and 1,336.2 ms became 288.3 ms. Reply bytes before the act fall from 83,661 to 15,474. The note labels these as observed single runs, run before then after and not randomized, and it claims no time for another run.\n\nAuthority, session, configuration and custody. Every press still reads fresh standing:\n\n- readInventory starts the three authority summaries together. A target skips only unrelated pins, definitions and roots.\n- #exactSnapshot derives a private context. It never replaces the ordinary catalogue, clears the stale flag or raises a list generation, and first-press.test.ts witnesses each of those three.\n- #perform still runs the target, definition, action policy, captured-view admission, signing and custody checks.\n- The Native revocation case removes destination.read-token after the card opens. The press then answers unknown-tool and signs nothing, so a retained read session grants no act.\n- #credential reuses the context only while the configuration digest matches, and it rechecks the digest on each poll.\n- ReadSessions keys a completed credential by service, signer key and the full membership reference, and reuse rechecks the returned claims and the ten-second margin.\n- Pending issuance and refusal cooldown stay per reader. forget drops the entry, so a late reply cannot install itself.\n- The reads.test.ts owners cover concurrent issuance, full-reference binding, forget during issuance, local cooldown and fallback, and eviction after 64 identities. Three named controls fail by assertion with their guards removed.\n\nCompanion 9abee3a0. The Native signer case now reads the Needs You list for each actor row. The case asserts that the list attributes the opening entry's signer, labeled **Opening act signed by**, not the viewer or the later writer. The note explains why this question fixture supplies no separate Work row, and the shared path is RepoInAi.#rows. That meets the conditional witness at this owning edit.\n\nThe gates under docs/testing.md. Gate 7b691a39 reads \"exit 1\", and its sole failure is the Native foreign-incarnation request count: 83 observed against 82 expected. The fix at 3e2c000b changes production code, so it correctly took a new full gate instead of the isolated-repair rule. Gate 3e2c000b also reads \"exit 1\". Its sole failure is the plain stand-in that lacks hasHeld, which threw and reached its unchanged 60-second deadline, and Native never ran. The repair 2f825e32 adds three lines to that one stand-in. scope-proof.json records that file as the only changed path, all other test bytes unchanged, and no importer. The follow-up exits 0 for the compiler, the whole four-case owner, compatibility preparation and the unreached Native stage. Native passes 1,029 cases with two skips. The pair meets the isolated-repair rule. Both full gates stay failed.\n\nCI. Card workflow 41424913952 succeeds at 3e2c000b. After that commit, the head changes only declared-members.test.ts and the two notes paths. None of them is a Card workflow path, so 3e2c000b is the last commit that could produce a run, and every card input is byte-identical at the head. The head adds packages/mcp/src/service.ts to both path filters, and docs/testing.md now names service.ts, actor-cards.ts and change-view.scope.test.ts as citation owners, as ruling e9c812f9 requires.\n\nEvidence. The manifest hashes to 7d30a2d8…a1e1, as the request states. All 269 files in its 11 units match their sizes and digests, no unit holds an unlisted file, and each unit's SHA256SUMS matches its manifest hash and passes. All 20 table digests match manifest entries. No evidence file is writable. The credential-pattern scan finds no match, and the regeneration wrote nothing into the units.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The cache shares completed credentials only, and each reader keeps its own transport, pending requests, cooldown and counters. That keeps one closed or failed collection from affecting another. One narrowing deserves a later look, but it does not block this head. readMembershipDisplay now returns null whenever this reader has held some incarnation of the scope and not this one. The service's reader lives as long as the process. If a held membership gains a new incarnation while the process runs, the member display stays empty until restart. Before this head, it recovered once the old session ended. The display fails safe and grants nothing, so the cost is display only. A later owner edit could compare against the configured membership instead of reader history.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The cache lives only in process memory and writes no token to disk. The new isScopeId check refuses a non-scope target before any read. Fresh standing, target, definition, captured view and custody still gate every act, and the Native revocation case proves the gate holds with a retained credential. Whole Native and CI logs stay private, and the units keep only their hashes and terminal extracts.\n\nSimplification: no required change. #deriveSnapshot is a direct split of snapshot(), and the exact path adds one method and one optional parameter. The member-display guard costs one condition.\n\nLimits stay explicit: no claim for generic or ordinary card acts, no new person-operated Desktop timing (1a44f042), no rendering or refresh change (76a1c020), no diff truncation or design change (e4d0cfed, 353a0ec0), and no deployment. A local stdio process takes the change when it runs the new source, and the planner decides any deploy after landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:edbedff4a4dfcbbb04556c5cfccfb4d0666b0018","binding":"assigned","head":"626d8551b676a08203264552fbe4d5044850cc2d","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f0f9c8394d919bd31152f00c31fd1f848bc9d2e7\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:097c35b0817ec94c25e01fe2adcc338c77da2475\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f0f9c8394d919bd31152f00c31fd1f848bc9d2e7","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}